    "## A4. How this session is built\n",
    "\n",
    "### The big picture\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌── COURSE REPOSITORY  (you pull it; you do not edit it) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│                                                                                                          │\n",
    "│ module01/providers_utils.py   THE TOOLS (reads .env on import: load_dotenv(override=True))               │\n",
    "│    groq_client · gemini_client · ollama_client     one client per provider, same OpenAI library          │\n",
    "│    list_gemini_models · pick_gemini_model          ask Google which Flash models exist, pick one         │\n",
    "│    ask(client, model, system, user, ...)           THE one function: one call, any provider              │\n",
    "│    classify_ticket(...) + CLASSIFIER_SYSTEM        ask() specialised: ticket in, one label out           │\n",
    "│                                                                                                          │\n",
    "│ module01/tickets_data.py      THE DATA                                                                   │\n",
    "│    CLEAR_TICKETS      3 tickets with an obvious label (billing / technical / general)                    │\n",
    "│    BORDERLINE_TICKETS 3 tickets that could honestly be two labels   ── the temperature sweep             │\n",
    "│                                                                                                          │\n",
    "│ module01/s11_providers.ipynb  ◄── YOU ARE HERE                                                           │\n",
    "│ module01/reading_providers.md, terms_s11.md    the pre-read and the terms table                          │\n",
    "│ tests/test_s11.py             the checkpoint: 6 offline tests + 2 live tests (Groq, Gemini)              │\n",
    "│ .env.example                  the template you copied to .env in Session 2 (Gemini block added)          │\n",
    "└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "                         │ the notebook imports the tools; the tools read ▼ your .env\n",
    "┌── YOUR MACHINE  (yours; never committed) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│ .env           BASE_URL · API_KEY · MODEL (Groq)   GEMINI_API_KEY · GEMINI_MODEL (Gemini)                │\n",
    "│ Ollama         optional; listens on http://localhost:11434 ; model llama3.2:3b                           │\n",
    "└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "                         │ every ask() becomes one web request ▼\n",
    "          Groq API (api.groq.com)      Gemini API (generativelanguage.googleapis.com)      Ollama (your laptop)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "No work-repository file is written today. What you produce is on your screen (answers, token counts, the sweep) plus four reflection answers in section 7.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What happens to one prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    " \"What is an EMI?\"            \"You are a terse assistant...\"         client = groq / gemini / ollama\n",
    "        │ user                        │ system (may be \"\")                   model = \"openai/gpt-oss-20b\" ...\n",
    "        ▼                             ▼                                      │\n",
    "   ask(client, model, system, user, temperature=0.0, max_tokens=200, stop=None)\n",
    "        │\n",
    "        │ 1. build the messages list   [ {system: ...} (only if system is not \"\"),  {user: ...} ]\n",
    "        │ 2. build the settings        model, messages, temperature, max_tokens (+ stop, only if given)\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "   client.chat.completions.create(**settings)  ──►  POST  <BASE_URL>/chat/completions  ──►  provider\n",
    "                                                                                              │\n",
    "        ┌──────────────────────── the reply comes back in the SAME shape from every provider ◄┘\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "   { \"text\": r.choices[0].message.content,\n",
    "     \"prompt_tokens\": ..., \"completion_tokens\": ..., \"total_tokens\": ... }      ◄── what you print\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "`classify_ticket()` is the same path with a fixed system message (`CLASSIFIER_SYSTEM`) and `max_tokens=1000` (a ceiling with room for a reasoning model's hidden thinking: with 10, `gpt-oss-20b` used the whole budget thinking and replied with nothing); it then cleans the reply and checks it is one of three allowed labels.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The helpers you will call, and what each does\n",
    "\n",
    "| Helper | Lives in | You give it | It gives back | Used in section |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `groq_client()` | providers_utils | nothing (reads `BASE_URL`, `API_KEY`) | a client for the provider in `.env` (Groq by default) | 1 |\n",
    "| `gemini_client()` | providers_utils | nothing (reads `GEMINI_API_KEY`) | a Gemini client; `RuntimeError` if the key is missing | 1 |\n",
    "| `ollama_client()` | providers_utils | nothing | a client for `localhost:11434/v1` (does not check Ollama runs) | 1 |\n",
    "| `list_gemini_models()` | providers_utils | nothing (asks Google live) | the chat-capable Flash model names your key can see | 1 |\n",
    "| `pick_gemini_model(names)` | providers_utils | that list | `gemini-flash-latest` if offered, else the highest plain `gemini-X.Y-flash`, else `None` | 1 |\n",
    "| `ask(client, model, system, user, ...)` | providers_utils | a client, a model name, two texts, optional `temperature`, `max_tokens`, `stop` | `{\"text\", \"prompt_tokens\", \"completion_tokens\", \"total_tokens\"}` | 2, 3, 4 |\n",
    "| `classify_ticket(client, model, text, temperature=...)` | providers_utils | a client, a model, one ticket | everything `ask()` returns, plus `label` and `valid` | 5 |\n",
    "| `CLEAR_TICKETS`, `BORDERLINE_TICKETS`, `ALL_TICKETS` | tickets_data | (data) | lists of `(ticket_id, text)` pairs | 5 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Three **under the hood** cells rebuild `pick_gemini_model`, `ask` and the label cleaning in `classify_ticket` in front of you, and check they match the real helpers, with no model call.\n",
