    "## 6. Switching provider — three lines, no code change\n",
    "\n",
    "### What and why\n",
    "This is the payoff. Open `.env`, comment the three Groq lines, and point `BASE_URL`/`API_KEY`/`MODEL` at a different provider. Nothing in `providers_utils.py` or this notebook changes. Re-run section 3 afterwards and compare. `groq_client()` reads whatever `.env` says, so those three lines decide which provider the whole course talks to.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The idea\n",
    "```\n",
    " .env today (Groq)                                   .env after switching (Ollama: the block already exists)\n",
    " ────────────────────────────────────────            ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    " BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1             # BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1\n",
    " API_KEY=gsk_...                                     # API_KEY=gsk_...\n",
    " MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b                            # MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b\n",
    "                                                     BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1\n",
    " # BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1                API_KEY=ollama\n",
    " # API_KEY=ollama                                    MODEL=llama3.2:3b\n",
    " # MODEL=llama3.2:3b\n",
    "```\n",
    "A `#` turns a line into a comment. The Ollama block is already in `.env.example`. For Gemini, write three lines yourself: `BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/`, `API_KEY=` your Gemini key, `MODEL=` the name section 1 printed after `using:`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Analogy — swap the plug, not the appliance.** Abroad, you change the adapter, not the laptop. `.env` is the adapter.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The steps, in order\n",
    "1. `code .env` in PowerShell (course folder).\n",
    "2. `#` before the three Groq lines; remove `#` from the three Ollama lines (or write the Gemini lines). Save.\n",
    "3. **Restart the kernel**: section 1's clients still hold the old address and key.\n",
    "4. Run section 1's setup cell, this cell, then section 3.\n",
    "5. **Switch back** to Groq afterwards and restart. The instructor pins `MODEL`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What the next cell does\n",
    "1. `importlib.reload(providers_utils)` runs the module again, and with it `load_dotenv(override=True)`, so `os.getenv` sees the new `.env` values.\n",
    "2. Re-imports `ask` and prints `BASE_URL` and `MODEL` so you can confirm the switch.\n",
    "\n",
    "A reload refreshes *settings*, not the clients already made: hence restart and re-run section 1. This cell calls no model and is unchanged."
