    "---\n",
    "# Part C · Wrap-up\n",
    "\n",
    "## C1. Summary\n",
    "- A **provider** is where a model runs; a **model** is which brain answers. Your code needs only three settings to talk to any OpenAI-compatible provider: `BASE_URL`, `API_KEY`, `MODEL`, all in `.env`.\n",
    "- `ask()` is one function for every provider: build a **messages list**, call `chat.completions.create`, read the text and the token usage. Only the client and the model name change.\n",
    "- The **system message** is the job description. Leave it out and the model uses its default style.\n",
    "- **Token counts** differ between providers for the same text (different tokenizers, hidden reasoning), and fewer tokens does not mean cheaper.\n",
    "- **max_tokens** is a ceiling that cuts, and on a reasoning model the hidden thinking counts too. **stop** is a tripwire that ends the reply at a given string.\n",
    "- **temperature** controls randomness. Decisions such as routing belong at 0 (or close to it): repeatable, though not guaranteed correct. Borderline inputs are where drift shows.\n",
    "- Model names change: verify them live (`list_gemini_models`).\n",
    "\n",
    "## C2. The words again\n",
    "\n",
    "| Term | One-line meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Provider | Where a model runs (Groq, Google, your laptop) |\n",
    "| Model | Which trained network answers, chosen by name |\n",
    "| OpenAI-compatible endpoint | Another vendor's address that accepts the same request shape |\n",
    "| `BASE_URL`, `API_KEY`, `MODEL` | Where, who, and which model: the three settings in `.env` |\n",
    "| Client | The Python object that holds one address and one key |\n",
    "| Provider-agnostic code | Code that works unchanged with any provider; only config changes |\n",
    "| Messages list and roles | Role/content pairs: system (job description), user, assistant |\n",
    "| Token usage | Prompt, completion and total tokens: the itemised bill |\n",
    "| temperature | The randomness dial for each next token |\n",
    "| top_p | A shortlist by probability: another dial for the same randomness |\n",
    "| max_tokens | The ceiling on reply length; it cuts, it does not plan |\n",
    "| Stop sequence | A string that ends the reply the moment it appears |\n",
    "| Drift | Same input, different output across runs |"
   ]
  },
